We are looking for strong **Senior / Middle Software Development Engineers** for a coding-heavy automated dependency management project at a developer platform company. The tool monitors outdated or vulnerable packages and creates pull requests to update them across multiple package ecosystems. The exact scope between the open-source tool and the platform remains to be confirmed.

**Requirements:**

* Strong hands-on coding and readiness to contribute from day one; practical coding ability matters more than years of experience;
* **Ruby proficiency** and ability to work with Go and Python;
* Confident everyday use of AI coding tools, including GitHub Copilot and agentic workflows;
* Git/GitHub workflows, including pull requests, code review and CI with GitHub Actions;
* Independent delivery, ownership of substantial work and good English for meetings, pull requests and issues.

**Responsibilities:**

* Contribute hands-on development to automated dependency management tooling;
* Work across languages and package ecosystems to support dependency updates;
* Collaborate through pull requests, code review and CI workflows;
* Take ownership of development tasks and ramp up quickly.

**Nice to Have:**

* Knowledge of package managers and ecosystems, including Bundler, npm/yarn, pip/Poetry, Go modules, Maven/Gradle, NuGet and Cargo;
* Experience with dependency management, semantic versioning and supply-chain security, including CVE/advisories;
* Docker;
* Open-source contributions, especially to relevant developer-platform or dependency-management repositories.

**Working Conditions:**

* Overlap: until 11 AM / 12 PM PT (Eastern Europe timezone works);
* Target start: ASAP. A couple of engineers who can start in 3-4 weeks and ramp up quickly; the rest can come in a second wave.

Farfetch is a leading global marketplace for the luxury fashion industry, connecting customers in over 190 countries with items from more than 50 countries and over 1,400 of the world’s best brands and charming boutiques from around the world. Farfetch opens a world of luxury for endless expressions of style, delivering a truly unique shopping experience and access to the most extensive selection of luxury on a global marketplace.

OPERATIONS

The Operations team serves as the backbone of our marketplace, seamlessly managing the entire order journey. From creating online content and ensuring secure payments to order fulfillment and delivery, while providing comprehensive customer and partner care, this team is relentlessly focused on improving the customer experience every single day.

THE ROLE

We are looking for a Customer Service Advisor (English & Arabic Speaker) to work in a relaxed environment and be part of a well-motivated, and growing team. Reporting to the Customer Service Manager, you will gain excellent experience, which will broaden as the team grows. You will have main responsibilities to ensure that the highest levels of customer service are delivered to both our consumers and partners and through every communication channel.

### **WHAT YOU'LL DO**

* Online Customer support via several channels including phone, email, and social media;
* Support of sales by being aware of current trends, styles, and availability of products;
* Liaising with boutiques, logistics, and other partners to ensure up to date delivery schedule;
* Ensuring that exemplary levels of Customer service are displayed at all times and our brand values are reflected in all interactions;
* Being front line voice and ears of Farfetch.

### **WHO YOU ARE**

* Native Arabic speaker;
* Has excellent verbal and written communication skills in English (essential minimum B2 level), both spoken and written
* Experienced in customer service ( 1 year), in a fashion environment;
* Proficient in the use of IT systems, both customer service specific and windows packages;
* Experience with written skills;
* Knowledgeable of fashion/fashion brands;
* Exceed customers' expectations;
* Available to work in Cairo (hybrid work).

